diff --git a/public/blog/tests/behat/profile_links.feature b/public/blog/tests/behat/profile_links.feature
new file mode 100644
index 00000000000..3c2a5bda5ec
--- /dev/null
+++ b/public/blog/tests/behat/profile_links.feature
@@ -0,0 +1,37 @@
+@core @core_blog
+Feature: Blog links in the user profile
+  In order to find personal and site blog entries
+  As a user
+  I need to see clear blog links in the Miscellaneous section of the profile
+
+  Background:
+    Given the following "users" exist:
+      | username | firstname | lastname | email                |
+      | testuser | Test      | User     | moodle@example.com   |
+    And the following "core_blog > entries" exist:
+      | subject       | body                | user     |
+      | Blog post one | Blog post content   | testuser |
+
+  Scenario: Both blog links are shown when blogs are enabled
+    Given I am on the "testuser" "user > profile" page logged in as "testuser"
+    Then I should see "View my blog entries"
+    And I should see "View site blog entries"
+
+  Scenario: The personal blog link opens the user's own blog entries
+    Given I am on the "testuser" "user > profile" page logged in as "testuser"
+    When I follow "View my blog entries"
+    Then I should see "User blog: Test User"
+    And I should see "Blog post one"
+
+  Scenario: The site blog link opens the site blog page
+    Given I am on the "testuser" "user > profile" page logged in as "testuser"
+    When I follow "View site blog entries"
+    Then I should see "Site blog"
+    And I should see "Blog post one"
+
+  Scenario: No blog links are shown when blogs are disabled
+    Given the following config values are set as admin:
+      | enableblogs | 0 |
+    When I am on the "testuser" "user > profile" page logged in as "testuser"
+    Then I should not see "View my blog entries"
+    And I should not see "View site blog entries"
